# Source: en.wiktionary.org, https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/diwrnod.
# diwrnod (masculine), plural diwrnodau, is the COUNTABLE day -- the
# word a numeral takes ("tri diwrnod", attested on cy.wikipedia.org).
# dydd (masculine), plural dyddiau, is the uncountable daytime and the
# head of every weekday name; both are read here because a duration
# phrase may use either.  Soft d -> dd after a trigger.
# Soft-mutated surfaces are listed beside the radical: Welsh changes a
# word's first letter after a preceding trigger.  Mutation table:
# en.wikipedia.org, "Welsh mutation".
# Singular only: the form a count of one takes.
diwrnod
ddiwrnod
dydd
ddydd
